course: dictionary
lesson: 10623
title: Unfertilised: not joined, so no new life
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Look at the parts of the word. Un- means not, and fertilised means joined with something so that new life can start. So unfertilised means not joined, so it cannot grow into a new animal or plant.
explain: «Some rainforest poison frogs carry their tadpoles up to little pools, and some mothers come back to feed them unfertilised eggs, because the tiny pool has almost no other food.» The eggs are fed to the tadpoles as food, which tells you they are not going to grow into babies.
explain: «The yolk of an unfertilised hen's egg is often called a single cell, full of food for a growing chick.» The clue is in the words: it is full of food for a chick, but it is unfertilised, so no chick will grow from it. Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence: "an egg that has not joined with a sperm cell" still makes sense.
fact: Unfertilised means not joined, so it cannot grow into a new animal or plant.
fact: An egg is unfertilised when no sperm cell has joined with it.
fact: The eggs we buy in shops are usually unfertilised, so they never hatch into chicks.
fact: A flower is unfertilised when it has not received pollen, so it cannot make a seed.
fact: Unfertilised soil or fields have had no fertiliser (plant food) added.
exercise: What does unfertilised mean? | Very large and very old | Joined together and ready to grow | Cooked and ready to eat | *Not joined, so it cannot grow into a new life
exercise: «The yolk of an unfertilised hen's egg is full of food for a growing chick.» Will this egg hatch into a chick? | Yes, if it is turned every day | *No, it cannot grow into a chick | It depends on the shop | Yes, if it is kept warm for three weeks
exercise: Which flower cannot make a seed? | A flower in a vase of water | *An unfertilised flower | A flower in full bloom | A flower that has had pollen
test: What does unfertilised soil mean? | *Soil with no fertiliser (plant food) added | Soil that has been watered with rain | Soil full of stones and sand | Soil that has been dug up by worms
test: Which egg is unfertilised? | An egg with a chick growing inside it | An egg that has hatched into a chick | An egg that has been hard-boiled and is ready to eat | *An egg where no sperm cell has joined with it
exam: «The yolk of an unfertilised hen's egg is often called a single cell.» What does unfertilised tell you about the egg? | *It has not joined with a sperm cell, so it cannot grow into a chick | It is full of plant food | It is bigger than any other egg | It will hatch into a chick
